legend right
  **Notation**
  Solid line with open arrow: association (permanent reference, navigable)
  Hollow diamond: aggregation (group holds members)
  Filled diamond: composition (parts live and die with the whole)
  Dashed open arrow: dependency (transient use). Unlabelled dashed arrows from a controller or entity
  to a view, result or value object mean it creates that object; the others are labelled
  <<include>> or <<extend>>.
  **Notes**
  Packages Boundary, Control and Entity group the classes by role.
  Types: String, Integer, Decimal, Boolean, Date, Time, DateTime, File, List<T>, Map<K, V>.
  Enumerations and value objects are listed at the bottom; view and result objects are
  returned by controllers and shown by WebFrontend.
  A Service needs 2 Engine Drivers, 1 Train Conductor and ceil(carriages / 2) each of
  Assistant Conductors and Cleaners.
  Controllers reach Staff, RosterWeek, Service, CrewPosition, Assignment and
  AvailabilityEntry through StaffGroup and RosterWeekGroup, so only the groups are linked.
  UC-07 "AvailabilityController" is named ManpowerAvailabilityController here.
  UC-12 "LateRequestController" is named LateRequestReviewController here.
  JobWithdrawalController handles UC-05 and its extension UC-14, since both hand
  an assigned job back to the reallocation queue.
  AllocationController handles UC-08 and UC-15. On a published roster, assign and
  unassign also notify staff, and unassign moves the job to the reallocation queue.
  ValidationController.findValidCandidates supplies the ranked candidates for
  UC-08, UC-11 and UC-15 (on-call staff first when reallocating).
  Manager-responsibility checks use StaffGroup.isResponsibleFor; week IDs and the
  availability window (UC-02, UC-07) come from RosterWeekGroup.
  RequestGroup (UC-05/06), ReallocationQueue (UC-13/14/15) and the RosterWeek queue
  operations (UC-11/12) all describe the reallocation queue.
  LateRequestQueue (UC-03) and LateRequestGroup (UC-12) both hold late requests.
  UC-13 adds cover periods through StaffGroup.addCover, while UC-03 reads them from
  CoverPeriodGroup: another consolidation candidate.
endlegend
